                          .-----------------------.
--------------------------|  What is The Quest ?  |--------------------------
                          `-----------------------'



  The Quest is simply the best user questionnaire ever coded for /X :)

 Seriously now...The Quest is the first fully interactive new user
questionnaire based on an editable "dictionary" and a "super" super wildcards
algorithm, with unbelievable new features never offered before and all
existing features splitted in the other doors.




                     .----------------------------------.
---------------------|  Why should you use The Quest ?  |--------------------
                     `----------------------------------'



 The Quest is not as easy to configurate as other Quest doors, but that's
the price for power. Power ? WHich power ? :)  Well, here is a summary:

 - The Quest is fully interactive.
 
 - The Quest is message based: messages will be sent to anyone you wish,
   even EALL's to warn about the arrival of a new user, and when a
   user has been kicked with the reason.
   
 - The Quest is fully configurable, brings new unbelievable features,
   is fast & pure ASM, etc... etc... I'm getting bored hehe ;)

 And all this is made possible via simple flags in the icon's tooltypes ! :)
Tooltypes ? TOOLTYPES ? ICON ?? AAAAAARGHHHH ?!?!?!   Hehe no, I also
provide in this archive a wonderful tool to edit icons tooltypes in your
favourite text editor ;)



                        .----------------------------.
------------------------|  Tooltypes & installation  |-----------------------
                        `----------------------------'


 Aha, the interesting part ! :)  Make a directory QUEST in your DOORS:
drawer (DOORS must be assigned) and copy the door in it + its icon. Put in
your BBS:Commands/BBSCmd drawer the door icon like for all doors. Location
will of course be: LOCATION=DOORS:QUEST/QUEST. Make a directory called
ANSWERS in this directory. And again... if you don't have the AEDoor.Library
by Sintax/WoT installed, don't expect the door to work !

 Sysops using /X v1.x -> 2.x will know better than me how to configurate
the whole thing.

 I advice you to call the door from the JOIN.TXT text (normally located in
BBS:Screens/Nodex/) like this: ~cc_Quest. It is not necessary to use an
MCI clearscreen command as the door will do it anyway.

         !!! I EVEN URGE YOU TO CALL THE DOOR FROM JOIN.TXT !!!
         
         Why ? Because if you call the door later, the user is previously
         recorded in the user.data, and if he is kicked, next time he
         calls The Quest WON'T be called as he IS member, and WON'T be
         able to control new users anymore.

 The characters xx and yy stand for any number from 0 to 4.294.967.295.
No limitation here so, but leading zeroes are not allowed (eg: 01).

 The following tooltypes must be edited in Quest.Info located in your Quest
drawer. You can use the TOOLTYPE util provided in the package to edit
them in your favourite text editor.



                          .----------------------.
                          |  Standard tooltypes  |
                          `----------------------'


  MUST_ANSWER=Yes/No

    Little flag to tell the door that the user MUST give an answer or may
    just press ENTER. Blanc lines are also detected.
    
    Default is YES.


  LEAVE_MSG=Yes/No

    If set to YES, the door prompts the ENTER MESSAGE command at the end
    of the questions to let the user write a bit about himself, his
    hobbies, etc... Kewl to see if the guy is nice or not, no ? :)
    No message is sent, it is just additional infos in the answers.

    Default is YES.


  LEAVE_MSG.TXT= ...

    This is a string or the full path to a text file to display just
    before this ENTER MESSAGE command, to tell the user what he should
    write. See the FLAG below. By default, the door will write this:
    
     "Please tell me about you, your hobbies, etc... now"


  LEAVE_MSG.FLAG=Line/Path

    Here you specify what the LEAVE_MSG.TXT is: a line to display or a
    path to a textfile. Don't forget this !
    
    Default is LINE.


  CHECK_ACCESS=xxx

    That's the access a user will need to be able to read the answers of
    new users. If you have this access level (or above) the door will ask
    you wether you want to answer the questions or look at other users'
    answers.
    
    Default is 240.


  BEGIN_TXT=Path

    Path to a text file to display instead of the default string at the
    beginning of the door. This string is:
    
      "USERNAME, remember that your validation depends on your knowledge..."


  END_TXT=Path

    The same, but for the end of the door ("thank you..." etc !).


  SYSOP.xx=Name

    You can use this tooltype to send a message to anyone you wish.
    If the name is EALL, the door sends an EALL message in any
    conference you wish to collect infos about the new user user from
    your users. Sysops will just receive a message telling them that
    there is a new user awaiting validation and his name. SYSOP.xx requires
    a path to a conference. Warning: EALL messages can be sent in several
    conferences, and therefore I added another tooltype. See the two
    tooltypes below.

    If SYSOP.1 doesn't exist, no message will be sent. The same if the
    paths given to the two tooltypes listed below are wrong.
    

  SYS_PATH.xx=Path

    This the path for the private message to Sysop.xx
    With or without terminating "/". The xx must be the same number as the
    one used for Sysop.xx
    
    A wrong path results in no message sent in this conference ;)
      

  EALL_PATH.xx=Path

    Here, you can give one or more path(s) to several conferences where
    the EALL message must be sent. The xx number stand for one conference,
    so if you wish to send an EALL message in 4 conferences, you will
    have EALL_PATH.1 to EALL_PATH.4
    
    A wrong path results in no message sent in this conference ;)


    e.g.: SYSOP.1=Diogenes
          SYS_PATH.1=BBS:Amigaworld
          SYSOP.2=Felix
          SYS_PATH.2=BBS:LamerLand
          SYSOP.3=EALL
          EALL_PATH.1=BBS:Amiga
          EALL_PATH.2=BBS:PC
          EALL_PATH.3=BBS:Mac
          EALL_PATH.4=BBS:Console
  

  KICK_NAME=Name

    As stated above in this document, the door will kick the new user
    under certain circumstances if you wish. These are:
    
     - The user has been previously member on the system (and so he was
       deleted and you do not wish to see him again);

     - The user gave an wrong answer to one of your questions. See
       the tooltypes about interactive analyse for more about this.
    
    The door can send a message to you or someone else, if you wish, to
    tell you about it, with the reason of the drop carrier procedure.
    Just give the name of the user who must receive the messages here.
    
    If this tooltype or the following one does not exist, or if the
    path given in the following tooltype is wrong, no message will be sent.
  

  KICK_PATH=Path

    This is the path to the conference where the messages about the
    drop carrier procedures must be sent. If wrong, no message is sent.
  
  
  PREVIOUS=Kick/Warn/Dummy

    Hehe, another cool one ;) If the user hasn't sysop access, the door will
    check wether he already answered the questionnaire or not. If well, we
    can assume he was deleted. If the flag is:
    
     - KICK, the door will drop a carrier on the user;

     - WARN, the door will simply tell the user that there's few chances for
       him to be validated;

     - DUMMY, no action is taken. Peace & love he ! 8-)
    
    In the KICK and WARN cases, defaut sentences will be displayed to the
    user, but you can of course use yours ;) See PREVIOUS.TXT and
    PREVIOUS.FLAG.
    
    Default is KICK.


  PREVIOUS.TXT= ...

    Type here the sentence to display, or the full path to a textfile,
    for the kick/warn previous user procedures. PREVIOUS.FLAG will tell the
    door what it is.


  PREVIOUS.FLAG=Line/Path

    Type here what PREVIOUS.TXT is: a sentence or the path to a text
    file.
    
    Default is LINE.


  SHOW_BOARDS=Yes/No      

    At the end of the quest, the door asks the user wether he wants to
    see other BBS's numbers (those are mine and two other cool boards).
    If you don't want the door to ask that, simply put NO.
    
    Default is YES.


  QUESTION.xx= ...

    This is where you type your questions ! You'll have to replace "xx" with
    a number, as usual.


  FLAG.xx=Comment/Question/Dummy
  
    Tells the door what QUESTION.xx is cause it can obviously be
    something else too ;)

     - QUESTION: means it is a... question ;-)  With the consequence
       that an answer is awaited. Use the LINES.xx tooltype to tell the
       door how many lines the user will have to answer.
       
     - COMMENT: means no answer will be awaited, the string will be
       displayed as well and then the next question if there is one.
       
       It's useful in this case for example:
       
        QUESTION.1=What do the following abreviations mean ?
        FLAG.1=Comment
        QUESTION.2=FLT
        QUESTION.2=SR
    
     - DUMMY: no action will be taken. This is useful if you want to display
       a textfile and nothing else using the tooltype TEXT.xx=Path
    
    Default is QUESTION.


  TEXT.xx=Path
  
    This an additional text file you can display just between the
    question/comment and the answer line. If FLAG.xx=DUMMY, the door
    only displays this text file and jumps to the next question.
    
    Just in case you wanted to have a lovely bear in the middle of the
    questionnaire or pictures for those who can't read ;-)


  LINES.xx=xx
  
    Tells the door how many lines to use for an answer.

    e.g.: you ask the names of 3 boards the user calls for the question 4,
          use LINES.4=3

    Default is 1.



                      .---------------------------------.
                      |  Interactive analyse tooltypes  |
                      `---------------------------------'


  COMPARE.xx.yy= ...
    
    Here you type an answer you think you could get from the user.
    Different procedures are possible when the user gives the awaited
    answer. See REP.xx.yy
    
    xx refers to the question number and yy is the number of the awaited
    answer for this question.
    
    A very important point to know is that the door will use YOUR
    indications to analyse the answers. Therefore, think twice before
    writing them, the door is limited by your mistakes ;-)
    
    The door uses a "Super" super wildcards algorithm in order to be able
    to work on complete sentences and even paragraphs. It is of course not
    case sensitive. If you know what super wildcards are, you've already
    understood how it all works ;)
    
    If you think that the user could answer "trader" for example, write
    *trad* to be sure, and it will not matter if he writes "TRadINg" or
    whatever ! You can imagine complete sentences: *cod*but*not*good*
    Or more interesting...:
    
      You ask the user wether he has an Amiga. If not, you'll kick him.
     
       *no*but*      could mean he will have one...
    
    Cut the words the most you can to be sure, there can be lotsa
    possibilities: coder, coding, code - not, no, nope, nooo - etc.... :)
    
    When an answer corresponds to your COMPARE string, no further
    comparisons are made after the REP procedure !
    
    Just "*" will mean... all answers are good.


  REP.xx.yy=Comment/Kick/Question

    That's what the door will do IF the corresponding COMPARE string
    was found in the answer:
    
     - COMMENT:  just displays a string or a textfile to the user.
                 See TEXT.xx.yy tooltype below.
     
     - KICK:     displays a string or a text file to the user and drops a
                 carrier on him.
                 See TEXT.xx.yy tooltype below. If not specified,
                 default string is: "ACCESS DENIED."
     
     - QUESTION: displays a string or a text file and waits for an answer.
                 See TEXT.xx.yy and LINES.xx.yy tooltypes below.
                 It is NOT possible here to display a text file, so
                 will be the usage of FLAG.xx.yy obsolete.
     
    There is no default. If none of these is given, no action will be taken.
    

  TEXT.xx.yy= ...

    A string or a path to display for the corresponding REP.xx.yy
    procedure. FLAG.xx.yy tells the door what it is.


  FLAG.xx.yy=Line/Path

    Used to tell the door wether TEXT.xx.yy is a string or a textfile
    to display as usual.
    
    Default is LINE.


  LINES.xx.yy=xx

    As for LINES.xx, this tells the door how many lines you want for
    the answer to REP.xx.yy. WARNING: This of course works ONLY if
    REP.xx.yy=QUESTION (default).



In practice it's very easy, look at this and get rid of your last
questions ! ;-)


MUST_ANSWER=Yes
SYSOP.1=Diogenes
SYS_PATH.1=BBS:Amigaworld
SYSOP.2=eall
EALL_PATH.1=BBS:Amigaworld
KICK_NAME=Diogenes
KICK_PATH=BBS:Amigaworld
SHOW_BOARDS=No
#
QUESTION.1=What is your speciality ? (Coder/Gfx/Music/Trader)
COMPARE.1.1=*cod*
COMPARE.1.2=*gfx*
COMPARE.1.3=*grap*
COMPARE.1.4=*mus*
COMPARE.1.5=*trad*
REP.1.1=Question
REP.1.2=Comment
REP.1.3=Comment
REP.1.4=Comment
REP.1.5=Comment
TEXT.1.1=In which language do you code ?
TEXT.1.2=Kewl, I draw like a pig ;-)
TEXT.1.3=Kewl, I draw like a pig ;-)
TEXT.1.4=Send me your best mod when you get a chance !
TEXT.1.5=Cool !
#
QUESTION.2=List the top 3 boards you call (3 lines)
LINES.2=3
#
QUESTION.3=What do the following abreviations stand for ?
FLAG.3=Comment
#
QUESTION.4=PDX
COMPARE.4.1=*Paradox*
COMPARE.4.2=*
REP.4.1=Comment
REP.4.2=Comment
TEXT.4.1=Correct.
TEXT.4.2=Wrong.
FLAG.4.1=Line
FLAG.4.2=Line
#
QUESTION.5=Do you have an Amiga ?
COMPARE.5.3=*no*
REP.5.1=Kick
TEXT.5.1=Access DENIED.
FLAG.5.1=Line
#
QUESTION.6=Can you EFFICIENTLY support this board ?
COMPARE.6.1=*no*
REP.6.1=Kick
TEXT.6.1=BBS:Screens/Node1/Kick.Txt
FLAG.6.1=Path



                       .-----------------------------.
-----------------------|  Last words about the door  |-----------------------
                       `-----------------------------'



 The door saves the questions, comments & answers only, your logos, ansis,
etc... won't appear in the file. It would take to much disk space and time.

 When a user looses carrier, the answer file is deleted, so the door
won't detect he already called and won't kick him the call after. At the
opposite, when the doors kicks someone, she DOESN'T delete the file ;-)

 The door will normally save 2 files: UserName.ans & UserName.mes. The
ANS file will contain the user's answers and the MES file will be the
last message written by the user. I can't swear this file will exist
since you can disable this option (!) and the Quest can be aborted at any
moment.




                             .----------------.
-----------------------------|  Future plans  |------------------------------
                             `----------------'



 * Possibility to tell the door another directory to save the answers

 * Users with EDIT_ACCESS enabled will have the possibility to edit the
   questionaire too ! This means that ya won't have to edit the icon's
   tooltypes anymore if you hate it ;)

 * Users with EDIT_ACCESS enabled will have the possibility to delete
   answers file too !

 * Multi-Questionaire possible to offer several languages. I was just lazy
   today ;)

 * A POINTS system ! The sysop will be able to set points for each question
   and the door will make a total of the points obtained by the user.
   This way, the sysop won't even have to read the answers ! If you see
   that the user got 0, then you can assume he's not good enuff ;)
   Or even let the door make statistics and decide alone !

 * Random questions... to avoid "hackers" and lamers who make an ascii
   capture of your questions and come back later.

 * Your suggestions ! ;)




